From: Stained Glass OS contributors
Subject: robocopy: a real robocopy

Wine's robocopy was a stub that failed every call (exit 16). Deployment,
logon and backup scripts use it, and so do package managers: Scoop moves
every package it extracts with `robocopy SRC DST /e /move`, so no Scoop
install could finish.

What scripts use: copy a tree, only what differs (size or time, New File /
Changed / Newer / Older / same), keeping timestamps and attributes; /S /E
/LEV:n; /MOV /MOVE; /PURGE /MIR; /XF /XD; /XO /XN /XC /XX /XL /IS /IT; /MAX
/MIN; /L; /CREATE; /A+: /A-:; /LOG /LOG+ /UNILOG /TEE and /NP /NFL /NDL /NJH
/NJS /NS /NC. Retry, thread, restart/backup-mode and copy-flag options are
accepted (data, attributes and times are always copied). robocopy's job
header, per-directory and per-file lines and summary table; its exit-code
bit mask (1 copied, 2 extras, 8 failures, 16 fatal).

Gate: test/robocopy-gate.sh (10 checks, 8 fail with the stub).
