+/*
+ * robocopy SOURCE DESTINATION [FILE ...] [OPTIONS]
+ *
+ * What deployment, logon and backup scripts use: copy a tree, only what
+ * differs (size or time), keep timestamps and attributes; /S /E /LEV:n;
+ * /MOV /MOVE (delete from the source after copying); /PURGE /MIR (delete
+ * from the destination what the source lacks); /XF /XD exclusions; /XO /XN
+ * /XC /XX /XL /IS /IT; /MAX /MIN; /L (list only); /CREATE; /A+: /A-:;
+ * /LOG /LOG+ /TEE and the /NP /NFL /NDL /NJH /NJS /NS /NC /NDL quietening.
+ * Options about retries, threads, restartable or backup mode, security
+ * and what to copy (/R /W /MT /Z /B /COPY /DCOPY /SEC ...) are accepted;
+ * data, attributes and timestamps are always copied.
+ *
+ * The exit status is robocopy's bit mask: 1 files were copied, 2 extra
+ * files or directories are in the destination, 4 mismatches, 8 some copies
+ * failed, 16 a fatal error (bad arguments, no source).
